{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/10/codegen_prompts/8.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/10`\n- 题号：`8`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/10/8.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"8\">\n- `description`：网格中每个彩色对象的轮廓形状被用作\"印章\"，盖印到由同色标记点指定的位置上；印章颜色由目标位置所在的背景分区决定而非来自原对象。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景由两种颜色组成：一条单像素宽的垂直分隔线（如 Grey）将网格分为左右两个区域，左区背景为一种颜色（如 Azure），右区背景为另一种颜色（如 Maroon）。\n  - 左区和右区各包含若干个单色实心对象（4-连通），每个对象使用唯一的非背景、非分隔线颜色。\n  - 在对象所在区域的对面区域中，有一个与该对象同色的单像素标记点。例如，左区的 Red 对象在右区有一个 Red 标记点。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个对象，提取其形状轮廓（即对象的完整像素集合相对于其左上角的偏移模式）。\n  - 找到对面区域中的同色标记点，以该标记点为锚（对应对象形状的左上角位置），将对象形状\"盖印\"到标记点所在区域。\n  - 盖印时颜色发生变换：不使用对象的原始颜色，而使用标记点所在区域的背景颜色。即左区对象印到右区时使用 Maroon，右区对象印到左区时使用 Azure。\n  - 原始对象和标记点在输出中都被保留不变，盖印的新形状叠加在目标区域上。若盖印像素超出网格或与分隔线重叠则截断。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成三步推理：首先识别分隔线将网格分为两个颜色不同的区域，其次理解同色标记点与对象的跨区配对关系以及形状复制的锚点逻辑，最后发现盖印颜色并非来自原对象而是取决于目标区域的背景色——这是一种\"入乡随俗\"的颜色替换规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/2faf500b, eval/581f7754, train/337b420f, train/6350f1f4, train/dc46ea44, train/b71a7747, train/20fb2937, train/5adee1b2\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2faf500b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2994\nmechanism=0.3661\nlexical=0.0121\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2faf500b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2faf500b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRemove each fracture marker line and push the surrounding object pixels one cell away from it.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid with 8-connected foreground objects made from a body color and a rarer marker color.\n- Each object has a non-square bbox; the marker pixels form one complete fracture line across the shorter bbox axis.\n\nRule\n- Erase all marker pixels.\n- For a wide object, each row has one marker; body pixels left of it shift one cell left and body pixels right of it shift one cell right.\n- For a tall object, each column has one marker; body pixels above it shift one cell up and body pixels below it shift one cell down.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker line is a crack through the object, so the two sides separate by one pixel perpendicular to the crack.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"8-connected body-color objects on the background, each crossed by a rarer marker-color fracture line\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the marker pixels; in each wide object shift body pixels one cell left/right away from the row marker, and in each tall object shift body pixels one cell up/down away from the column marker\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2979\nmechanism=0.3464\nlexical=0.0120\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"337b420f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2792\nmechanism=0.3367\nlexical=0.0115\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/337b420f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/337b420f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nKeep the larger sprite from each separated panel and overlay those sprites into one 5x5 canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a 5x17 grid: three 5x5 panels separated by one-cell black columns.\n- Each panel has the same background color and exactly one foreground color split into two 4-connected components.\n\nRule:\n- In each panel, discard the smaller foreground component and keep the unique largest component as the sprite.\n- Process panels left to right, placing each sprite at its panel coordinates on a 5x5 background canvas.\n- If a sprite would cover an already placed sprite, slide it by the unique nearest in-bounds offset that avoids overlap.\n\nKey insight:\n- The extra same-colored component in each panel is a distractor; the final answer is the non-overlapping overlay of the three largest components.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"largest 4-connected foreground object in each 5x5 panel\",\n  \"dst\": \"overlay onto one 5x5 canvas in left-to-right panel order\",\n  \"transform\": \"discard the smaller same-color object from each panel; when a later object overlaps earlier objects, slide it by the nearest in-bounds non-overlapping offset\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"5x17 input with separator columns -> 5x5 output\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6350f1f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2533\nmechanism=0.2801\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:sprite, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6350f1f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDecode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size\nsquare blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a\nuniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased\ncells that act as wildcards.\n\nRule\nInfer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a\nblock matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of\nthe sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.\nSeparator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.\n\nKey insight\nThe small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the\nuniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the\nopposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"regular block grid separated by black lines; each block is either a two-color sprite or a uniform blank block, with grey pixels as erasures\",\n  \"dst\": \"same block grid with the two block states swapped\",\n  \"transform\": \"infer the sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks; sprite-coded blocks become solid majority-color blocks, blank blocks become the sprite, and separator/erasure pixels become black\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"dc46ea44\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2593\nmechanism=0.3485\nlexical=0.0116\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:axis, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/dc46ea44.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dc46ea44.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the lower sprite and its pink guide into the upper panel, aligning the sprite to the guide's lower-left branch.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one full-width separator row.\n- Below the separator are exactly two foreground roles: a five-pixel guide marker and one monochrome sprite.\n- The guide marker has normalized shape {(0,2), (1,2), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1)} and starts immediately below the separator.\n\nRule\n- Clear the canvas to the background, preserving the separator row.\n- Translate the guide marker upward so its top row becomes row 0.\n- Move the sprite, preserving its color and shape, so the sprite bbox bottom-right aligns to the translated guide's lower-left branch.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker supplies the destination anchor: its lower-left branch cell is where the moved sprite's bbox bottom-right must land.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"monochrome sprite s below the separator\",\n  \"dst\": \"translated guide marker branch anchor d in the upper panel\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.bbox bottom-right aligns to d, the guide marker's lower-left branch after the marker shifts upward\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear the lower panel; shift the five-pixel guide marker to the top; stamp s without rotation or recolor\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"paint the shifted guide marker first, then stamp s so sprite pixels overwrite guide pixels on overlap\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b71a7747\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2610\nmechanism=0.3450\nlexical=0.0120\ncode_feature=0.2000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:axis, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b71a7747.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b71a7747.json\n</paths>\n<description>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
